# Channel sharing: the Meshtastic link, in both directions.
#
# This is the phone apps' onboarding path and the one thing the Brick could not do at all until
# now. Three things to watch:
#
#   1. The channel list, which has grown two rows under the slots. They are at the foot rather
#      than the head because they are about the *set* rather than about a channel, and because
#      the row somebody arrives here wanting is almost always a slot.
#   2. The share screen. The code takes every pixel of the body it can get, because how large
#      its modules are is most of whether a phone across the table reads it - and its scale is a
#      whole number of pixels, so it may not quite fill the room it was given. Under it, what is
#      in it, and then the link itself: last, dim, and wrapped rather than cut, because a link
#      with an ellipsis in it is not a link.
#   3. The code is black on white on every theme, which is the one colour pair in this client
#      that does not follow the palette. Watch it stay put as the theme changes around it. That
#      is not an oversight - several scanners, the one built into iOS among them, will not read
#      an inverted code at all, so a code that followed the dark theme would be a code half the
#      people it is shown to cannot scan.
#
# The other direction - a link typed in - is the keyboard and then the ordinary confirm sheet,
# both of which are filmed elsewhere; what is new there is the check in front of the sheet, and
# a refusal is not a thing a capture can show usefully.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

tab settings
hold 500

# Into Channels: eight slots, which is what a finished sync looks like - the firmware answers
# for every index, disabled ones included. The two rows this change adds are under them.
key down 11
key a
hold 1200
key down 8
hold 1800

# The code. Everything needed to join this radio - both channels, their keys, and the LoRa
# settings - as one square somebody points a phone at.
key a
hold 2600

# The same code on the light palette and on the one with a single accent, where every other
# colour on the panel moves and this one does not.
theme light
hold 2200
theme contrast
hold 2200
theme dark
hold 1400

key b
hold 800
